  "scope_notes": [
    "The two captures ran sequentially, with no other agent GPU workload. Each used five independent warmup frames before fresh initialization and all 25 measured live steps.",
    "This report replaces the obsolete tetrahedral twist-release timing report. It makes no before/after speedup claim and contains no measurements of that removed discretization.",
    "Nsight and NVTX overhead is included. Graph-mode timings and node-mode kernel shares come from separate runs of the same source, asset and workload.",
    "Zero explicit CUPTI lost records were reported; generic capture-end CUDA/NVTX/OS-runtime completeness warnings remain. Zero explicit loss does not establish perfect trace completeness.",
    "Raw capture coverage can include retained warmup events. GPU timing is restricted to measured NVTX frame intervals; overlapping graph intervals are unioned to avoid nested double counting. The graph capture has exactly 25 whole-graph events in measured frames, versus 30 in its complete raw database.",
    "Step host timings include check_status synchronization, position downloads, per-frame Gauss determinant validation and the final validation performed inside step. The first measured step also assembles and factors the system.",
    "Frames 1 and 2 create the two ping-pong outer graphs; frames 3 through 24 are their 22 replays. The inner conditional iteration graph also executes during the first step.",
    "Every render callback runs, including surface-edge GPU preparation, but NullViewer omits actual OpenGL drawing, encoding and readback. Asynchronous rendering kernels extending past an NVTX frame boundary are clipped by the scoped GPU accounting.",
    "The video presents 0.25 simulated seconds at 12 fps. Playback duration is not physics throughput; these profiled runs do not establish unprofiled real-time or interactive GUI performance."
